The boundary trace shows pydantic-core owns the actual walk and currently emits declared fields before extras; duplicate keys therefore overwrite in Python dict output and appear twice in raw JSON. The same bypass occurs for nested models when only the parent is dumped, so a root-only result patch would be incomplete. I’m checking the repository’s upstream history for an established minimal fix before choosing how to preserve nested behavior without mutating user instances.
